 "text": " Me and my kid are rebooting the Jaws series. Here's every plot from Jaws 5 to Jaws 10. Now remember, in Jaws 5 we started out with friggin' Shark 9-11 and then we learned the sharks are coming from a cave where they lay their eggs. The audience loved it. Rotten Tomatoes score 99, so we're running it back for Jaws 6. Fourth of July. Edgartown Harbor. The whole town is out on boats for the fireworks. Police Chief Brody, played by Pedro Pascal, is watching from the dark as a shock rams the fireworks barge during the grand finale. It tips sideways and every rock and fire straight across the harbor. Sailboats on fire. Bombs bursting in the air. It looks like the friggin' War of 1812 and no one can stop the recording of the national anthem that's playing over it. Police Chief Brody and Chief Oceanographer Jesse, played by Jesse Plemons, knows exactly what happened. The sharks are back and the radar shows them right under Edgartown Harbor. So Police Chief Brody hops back in the mechanical shark sub and follows them into a cave that ends right underneath Edgartown Bookstore. Same plan, same execution. They throw up the bait, blow the cave entrance, kick the kids out of the bookstore and drain the water. But here's what makes Jaws 6 even crazier. They realize something big is going on. How are these sharks making caves? Jesse's got a hunch. He runs some tests and guess what? The sharks are radioactive. They were never normal sharks. These were radioactive mutant sharks the whole time. But where are they coming from? Now, Police Chief Brody and Jesse have a whole new mystery to solve and that sets us up for Jaws 7.",
